  "query_preview": "../Friday through Sunday/...An area of low pressure \nremains southwest of Haida Gwaii Friday allowing for showers to \ncontinue over the panhandle. Similar to what we have been seeing, \nthe highest rain totals and heaviest rates look to remain over \nsouthern areas. There is a chance for isolated thunderstorms to \ndevelop across on Friday shortwave moves over the area. Similar \nconditions will continue into Saturday as the low moves eastward \nallowing for some easterly flow to continue into SE AK. Although \nthere is signs of convection, confidence on thunderstorm \ndevelopment remains low at the moment. If thunderstorms do \ndevelop, periods of gusty winds and heavier rain are likely to \noccur. We will continue to monitor as we get closer to the \nweekend.\n\nAs the low pressure system moves eastward, an area of higher \npressure takes its place in the gulf. This could help to create \nslightly warmer weather for late in the week. This will also help \nto create drier weather for the end of the weekend. High \ntemperatures are likely to reach into high 60s to the low to mid \n70s. Warmest locations look to be across the north where cloud \ncover will remain lower. As this higher pressure builds, it will \nalso allow for winds over the gulf to become northwesterly for the\nweekend. Strongest winds will be over the NE gulf into Icy Strait\nand Lynn Canal. Otherwise, overall winds remain on the lighter \nside, at or below 15 kts, for the long term forecast period.",
